! mcp_bootstrap_p175.strap -- THE PROGRAM-PROTECT FIXUP SCANNER, its
! error exits, its four VF work cells, and a SECOND COPY of the
! SIC/BD interrupt-slot pattern.  Printed page 175.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.182, header READ and not assumed:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD
! ID KE000045   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  175".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD READS 220606. <<<
! Rendered at 400 dpi across the full 6800-pixel width of the form:
! the word "LOCATION" at the right-hand end of the heading row is
! followed by SIX DIGITS, 220606.  Digits, not dashed rule -- the
! strokes are the same height as the "PAGE NUMBER 175" above them.
! That is IBM's own assembler stating LINE 1'S location, and line 1
! here IS a located row (220606.00), which is exactly the case
! docs/transcription_workflow.md says makes the field numbered.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIFTY-SIX PRINTED LINES, counted off the LINE column 1*..56* with
! no gap; line 56 is followed by blank paper to the foot of the
! form and line 1 is the first row under the heading rule.  NOTHING
! FELL OFF EITHER END.  (The survey read 34 rows, 220607.0..
! 220640.00.  It lost line 1 at the top, every row from 220640.00
! down -- the two DDs, the four VFs, the CNOP and the eight
! SIC/BD rows -- and the two comment cards.  22 rows short.)
!
! Two comment cards (lines 2 and 41) that compile nothing, 54 cards
! that compile: 34 half-word instructions, 13 full-word
! instructions, 2 DD words, 4 VF half words, and one CNOP that
! emits NOTHING because the counter is already word-aligned when it
! is read (which is why line 48 prints no location and no binary).
!
! THOSE COUNTS CHECK THEMSELVES AGAINST THE SPAN, so redo the sum
! rather than trusting it: the 13 full-word rows are the ones
! printing TWO half-word groups -- lines 1, 9, 14, 15, 17, 18, 19,
! 21, 22, 24, 26, 31, 33 -- and
!     34 + 13*2 + 2*2 + 4*1 = 68 half words = 34 words,
! while 0o220650 - 0o220606 = 0o42 = 34 words.  The two agree, so
! no row is miscategorised and none is missing.
!
! >>> THE PAGE IS CONTIGUOUS, 220606.00 .. 220650.00, NO HOLE. <<<
! No DR, no DRZ, no SLC of any kind, forward or backward.  Every
! one of the 20 labels lands on the location the page prints for
! it, FIRST TRY, with a single hard SLC at the top -- see the
! "JOIN" section for what that SLC is and is not.
!
!   lines  1      the tail of printed p.174's loop: "ST(BU),0.($2)
!                 -SAVE PATTERN WORD AT A(I)".  p.174's last row
!                 (its line 56, 220605.00, a FULL word
!                 "L(BU),0.($1)") ends at 220606.00, so this row is
!                 the one p.174's branch falls into.
!
!   lines  3-11   F STUP, the per-word setup and the bit-scan loop
!                 head F CKBT.  $3 walks the bit address of the
!                 pattern word (F LZCN), $4 the word being fixed
!                 (F ADC / F ALOC).
!
!   lines 12-18   F SVI / F SVT, the "save the interpreted word"
!                 arm: read the interrupt table entry S IT($4), ask
!                 whether it is an MCP store fixup, and store
!                 either the word or zero into A(I).
!
!   lines 19-34   F STN, the fixup-word arm: F STZ inserts, F SBD
!                 is the SIC-BD test, F INS does the insertion, and
!                 F BTCK is the loop bottom (CB+ back to F CKBT).
!
!   lines 35-40   the four error exits F ERRY, F ERRZ, F ERRX,
!                 F BIER -- all of which printed p.174 branches to.
!
!   lines 42-47   the work cells: two DD words and four VF half
!                 words.
!
!   lines 49-56   F WIT, four SIC/BD pairs.  THIS IS THE SAME
!                 PATTERN printed pp.110 and 111 carry at
!                 215044..215051, and decks/mcp_bootstrap_p111.strap
!                 line 334 already cites "p.175 BD,SIFAE" as the
!                 ONE outside witness for SIFAE's address.  That
!                 witness is hereby re-rendered and it holds:
!                 220645.40 prints "215471.04 00".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRIMARY SOURCE DRAWS THIS PAGE, LINE FOR LINE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! C22-6728-1 MCP System Analysis Guide, printed p.222, "The Fixup
! Routine", is the whole of this page in English and it is TYPESET
! -- a different document, not this drum:
!
!   "Enter $FIXUP at FFXP (Figure 127) and save the return address
!   in STIC.  Compute the effective parameter addresses, checking
!   for legal boundaries.  If not within PP bounds, exit via the
!   error routine (SDISP) with a type 9 error code."
!        -> that is printed p.174, whose rows branch to this
!           page's F ERRX (line 38, LVI,$14,S FORBD) -- and
!           printed p.107 line 14 names S FORBD "- 9".
!
!   "Store the pattern word from B(J) into A(I), if the latter is
!   non-zero."                      -> LINE 1, "-SAVE PATTERN WORD
!                                      AT A(I)".
!   "Remove all extraneous ones from the pattern word, and return
!   via $RET if the result is zero, otherwise, save the count of
!   the number of fixups to be handled."
!        -> p.174's "C(BU),FBMSK -REMOVE UNWANTED ONES ONLY",
!           this page's F BMSK (line 43) and F ALOC (line 44,
!           "-TO SAVE AOC"), and line 6's "BXCZ,K SUPP -RETURN IF
!           PATTERN WORD IS ZERO", which IS the $RET.
!
!   "At FCKBT, adjust the control indices and test the pattern
!   bits.  For each one bit, save the contents of the relative
!   interrupt table location at A(1), if A(J) is non-zero."
!        -> LINES 8-19: F CKBT, the BB on the pattern bit, and
!           the S IT($4) load/store arm.
!
!   "Test the corresponding fixup word and if illegal, exit via
!   the error routine (SDISP) with a type 19 error code."
!        -> LINES 20-25 and 33-36: the two KFI tests, BAE,F ERRY,
!           and F ERRY's "LVI,$14,S FIXP" -- printed p.107 line 24
!           names S FIXP "-19 ILLEGAL FIXUP WD", which is the
!           manual's "type 19" to the digit.
!
!   "Store the legal fixup word directly into the relative
!   interrupt table location and decrement the count.  When the
!   count becomes zero, return via $RET, otherwise continue at
!   FCKBT."
!        -> LINES 26-32: F INS's "ST(BU),S IT($4) -INSERT FIXUP
!           INTO INTERPT TABLE", F BTCK, "CB+,$4,F CKBT" and
!           "B,K SUPP -UPDATE $4 AND RETURN IF CNT ZERO".
!
!   "Exits To: SDISP ... Type 9 - parameters not with PP bounds /
!   Type 19 - illegal FIXUP word"
!        -> LINES 39-40, "SIC,S DISIC" then "B,S DISP -EXIT TO
!           ERROR ROUTINE".
!
! Nothing in the deck is INFERRED from that prose -- every bit
! comes off the listing -- but the two agree box for box, which is
! the strongest statement available that no row was misread into a
! different instruction.  The manual also names the entry point
! FFXP, which this page does NOT define: expect it on printed
! p.174 (its index spells it "FRXP", OCR for FFXP).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN, BOTH ENDS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIS PAGE PRINTS NO "SLC" AT ALL, so the deck must assert an
! origin and `listing_oracle` cannot check it (workflow "WHAT THE
! ORACLE CANNOT SEE" item 2: a hard SLC overrides the arriving
! counter silently).  TWO INDEPENDENT READINGS SAY 220606.00 and
! they are not the same reading:
!
!   (a) the heading row's own LOCATION field, 220606, printed by
!       IBM's assembler, read off the page at 400 dpi;
!   (b) docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt's OCR of printed p.174 --
!       a DIFFERENT PAGE, so a legitimate witness -- whose last
!       row is "5# 220605.0C  C. 81 C0000.2C 5C  L(RU),O.( #1)",
!       a FULL word at 220605.00 which ends at 220606.00.
!
! (a) gives no bit offset and (b) is an OCR, but they agree on the
! word and line 1's own LOCATION column reads 220606.00 at 900 dpi.
!
! >>> A WARNING FOR WHOEVER MERGES THIS BEFORE pp.169-174 LAND. <<<
! Measured, not guessed: merging pp.99-168 + this page succeeds
! ("671 defined, 63 external") and reports ZERO unaccounted words
! -- but only because this deck's hard SLC is a FORWARD SLC, so
! strap_asm records 220377..220605 (135 words, 0o207) as a
! legitimate SLC skip.  THOSE 135 WORDS ARE pp.169-174's, not a
! hole.  check_mcp_body_image.py will therefore stay green across
! a gap it should not be green across until those pages land, and
! a reader who sees "every_word_accounted_for = 0" in between
! should not read it as "nothing is missing".
!
! >>> PREDICTION FOR printed p.176. <<<  Line 56 is a HALF word at
! 220647.40, so THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 220650.00.  If
! p.176's first located row is not 220650.00 (or its heading-row
! LOCATION field is not 220650), one of us is wrong.
!
! >>> PREDICTION FOR printed p.174. <<<  Its counter must arrive at
! 220606.00, i.e. its last located row is a FULL word at 220605.00.
! Its page should also DEFINE nothing this page defines and should
! REFERENCE F STUP (220607.00), F PTWD (220640.00), F BMSK
! (220641.00), F ALOC (220642.00), F ADC (220643.00), F ERRZ
! (220636.00) and F ERRX (220636.40) -- the volume OCR of p.174
! prints rows for all seven.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPH CALLS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) EVERY ROUND GLYPH ON THIS PAGE IS AMBIGUOUS AND I CHECKED
!     THAT RATHER THAN ASSUMING IT.  Rendered at 1800 dpi, line
!     48's "CNOP" prints C-N-O-P with the C and the O IDENTICAL,
!     and line 45's "F LZCN  VF,0.0" prints its C and its two 0s
!     identically.  So on this page O, C and 0 are one shape and
!     "it looks like a C" carries NO information in a letter field.
!     D is the exception and is readable: it has the straight left
!     stem and squared corners the workflow describes, and line
!     46's "F ADC" shows it beside a round C in the same name.
!
! (2) THE OCTAL FIELDS SETTLE THEMSELVES.  Lines 1, 12, 17, 18, 19,
!     21, 22, 24, 26, 27, 28, 33, 35 and 44-47 all print a C
!     somewhere in a field that can only hold 0-7 ("COCCOO.CO 82",
!     "CCCOCC.OC+").  Every one is a 0.  That is the page dropping
!     ink on round glyphs, not a reading.
!
! (3) B vs 8: line 8 prints "220643.46 BO" and line 43 prints
!     "BFFFFFFOCOO".  BOTH are B.  Line 8 is settled by the
!     assembler (V+ produces B0); line 43 is settled OUTRIGHT by
!     its own BINARY OUTPUT, which prints the 22 octal digits
!     0000000277777777600000 -- and 0xBFFFFFF0000 right-justified
!     in 64 bits IS 0o277777777600000, while 0x8FFFFFF0000 is
!     0o217777777600000.  The listing checks its own hex literal.
!
! (4) D0 vs DC on lines 1, 18 and 26.  All three are ST and all
!     three print "DC" to the eye.  D0: the same byte printed p.168
!     line 8 settled at 1800 dpi, the counterpart of the 50 that
!     lines 14, 17 and 19 print for L on this same page with the
!     IDENTICAL operand word 000000.20, and what the assembler
!     produces for ST.  Three witnesses, one of them this page's
!     own rows four lines apart.
!
! (5) WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE, AND IT IS A SPELLING, NOT A BIT.
!     TWO names turn on a round glyph that (1) says is unreadable,
!     and NO page and NO manual outside this one prints them:
!
!       F BTCK (lines 27, 32)     F OVF (lines 47, 8)
!
!     I read them BT CK ("bit check", the loop bottom to F CKBT's
!     loop head) and O VF ("the VF holding one" -- F OVF holds
!     0.01 and line 8 adds it to the bit address, comment
!     "-INCREMENT B.A. +0.01").  Both readings of each ARE valid
!     symbol names, so rung 3 of the ladder (hand both to the
!     assembler) is SILENT here, and every reference is on this
!     page so no address check can see the difference.  THESE TWO
!     REST ON ENGLISH ALONE.  The ladder was walked to the end for
!     both: rung 1 (the comment column) says nothing, rung 2 was
!     GREPPED AND CAME BACK EMPTY -- "BTCK" and "OVF" appear in
!     none of docs/ocr/C22-6678-1, C22-6728, C22-6728-1,
!     C28-6129, C28-6379-0, J22-6559, N22-0085 or X28-6131.
!
!     F CKBT WAS IN THIS LIST AND IS NO LONGER: rung 2 FIRES for
!     it.  The TYPESET C22-6728-1 printed p.222 says, in prose,
!     "At FCKBT, adjust the control indices and test the pattern
!     bits" and "otherwise continue at FCKBT", and its symbol
!     index lists FCKBT, FERRX and FERRY together.  Different ink,
!     different press, genuinely independent of this drum.
!     F ERRY and F ERRX are settled the same way, twice over.
!
!     F LZCN is not in the list: its comment prints "LZC" in
!     English prose on lines 45 and 46 and printed p.174's own
!     comment reads "LEFT ZEROS COUNT", which is rung 1.
!     F ALOC, F ADC, F PTWD, F BMSK, F STUP and F ERRZ are not in
!     it either: printed p.174 prints a reference to each.
!
! (6) F SVI/F SVT/F STN/F INS/F STZ/F SBD/F ERRY/F BIER/F WIT carry
!     no ambiguous glyph at all.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every line number carries the ordinary trailing asterisk ("1*",
! "56*").  THREE ROWS CARRY A SECOND ASTERISK AFTER THE LOCATION:
! lines 1 (220606.00), 19 (220621.40) and 36 (220635.40).
!
! BE PRECISE ABOUT WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT BEAR ON.  printed
! p.147's proposal was "every printed SLC,$ row carries it", i.e.
! SLC => asterisk.  THIS PAGE HAS NO SLC AT ALL, so it is silent
! on that proposition and does NOT refute it; printed p.151 did
! that.  What these three rows show is the CONVERSE failing --
! asterisk does not imply SLC -- and that is CORROBORATION of
! printed p.111, whose lines 27 and 50 are ordinary BD/SIC rows
! carrying the mark.  Here line 1 is the page's first row, line 19
! is a label row (F STN) and line 36 is neither (a plain
! "B,F BIER"), so no property shared by the three suggests itself.
! RECORDED, NOT EXPLAINED.  Nothing the mark touches changes a
! compiled bit, and I propose no rule from one page.
!
! The LINE column also carries a second, right-hand ruler of
! numbers 1..20 running UPWARDS beside the bottom twenty rows; that
! is the form's own pre-printed carriage scale, not listing output.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> ASSEMBLER LIMITATION HIT: A CARD-LEVEL "(16)" RADIX PREFIX
! >>> REFUSES A LITERAL CONTAINING A-F.  ONE SUBSTITUTION, LINE 43.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The page prints
!
!     F BMSK   (16)DD(BU),BFFFFFF0000
!
! and `strap_asm` refuses it:
!
!     line N: cannot parse DD literal 'BFFFFFF0000'
!             (only decimal and (radix)digits are supported)
!
! It is NOT that the card-level radix prefix is unimplemented --
! "(16)DD(BU),10" assembles and yields 0o20, so the prefix IS
! applied.  `parse_dd_literal` (strap_asm.py, the
! `_DD_RADIX_LITERAL` regex and the `int(field, 10)` fallback under
! it) runs BEFORE the card's entry radix is consulted, so a datum
! whose digits are all 0-9 survives and one containing A-F does
! not.  The bug is parse order, and the failing case is exactly the
! case the prefix exists for.
!
! A DD error aborts the WHOLE assembly, so "let the row fail" would
! have left all 56 rows unchecked -- the duplicate-label situation
! in another costume.  THE DECK THEREFORE WRITES THE EQUIVALENT
! INLINE FORM, LOUDLY:
!
!     printed:  (16)DD(BU),BFFFFFF0000
!     written:  DD(BU),(16)BFFFFFF0000
!
! Same radix, same digits, same word: the !CHECK below is the
! page's own 22 printed octal digits and it passes, which is what
! shows the substitution changed nothing but the card.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- ALL NINE WERE ALREADY LANDED BY OTHER PAGES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Not one is new, and each SYN below is copied in the form the
! DEFINING page's deck uses, so the merged image cannot disagree:
!
!   S IT    215023.00  p.110 label        (p.175 uses SIT($4))
!   S TIC   215265.00  pp.103/119/144
!   S IPT   215103.00  p.112 line 7 defines it
!   S IFA E 215471.00  p.111 line 334, whose ONE witness is this page
!   K SUPP  216242.00  p.128 "K SUPP NOP,K COMM R"
!   S DISP  217372.00  p.119 lines 43/46
!   S DISIC 217451.40  p.103 line 289
!   S FIXP  (16)0109   p.107 line 24 "-19 ILLEGAL FIXUP WD"
!   S FORBD (16)1009   p.107 line 14 "- 9 COMMUNICATION WITH"
!
! NONE of the nine is used in a position that takes a data
! description from the symbol: SIT appears only inside L(BU)/
! ST(BU)/TI cards that carry their own dds, SFIXP and SFORBD only
! in LVI, the rest only in B/BD/SIC.  So the pp.153-160 dds rule
! has nothing to bite on here, and no stand-in was needed: every
! external is a SYN, never a copy of a defining card.
!
! The two LVI constants are worth one line each, because the
! printed word is the whole of the check: line 35 prints
! "000411.35 01" and 0o411 = 0x0109 = SFIXP; line 38 prints
! "010011.35 01" and 0o10011 = 0x1009 = SFORBD.  Both agree with
! printed p.107's defining cards digit for digit, which is a real
! cross-page check and not a tautology -- p.107 is where they are
! DEFINED and this page only USES them.
!
! S IPT is checked three times over, which is why its SYN is safe:
! SIPT+20. prints 215127, SIPT+22. prints 215131 and SIPT+23.
! prints 215132, all three against SIPT = 215103 with the "+NN."
! read as DECIMAL WORDS.  Three equations, one unknown, no slack.
!
! K SUPP's and S DISP's BIT offsets are UNOBSERVABLE here (workflow
! item 1): a plain B prints target+.10 and shows only bit 32.
! Writing ".0" is this corpus's convention, not a reading.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

SIT     SYN, (8)215023.0             ! p.110 label; p.175 SIT($4)
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0             ! pp.103/119/144
SIPT    SYN, (8)215103.0             ! p.112 line 7 defines "S IPT"
SIFAE   SYN, (8)215471.0             ! p.111 line 334; THIS page is its witness
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0             ! p.128 line 3; bit offset unobservable
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0             ! p.119 lines 43/46; bit offset unobservable
SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40            ! p.103 line 289
SFIXP   SYN,(16)0109.0               ! p.107 line 24  -19 ILLEGAL FIXUP WD
SFORBD  SYN,(16)1009.0               ! p.107 line 14  - 9 COMMUNICATION WITH

        SLC, (8)220606.0             ! NOT PRINTED.  Asserted; see "THE JOIN"
        ST(BU),0.($2)                ! line  1 * -SAVE PATTERN WORD AT A(I)
!                                    ! line  2   comment card, a lone "-"
FSTUP   LV,$3,FLZCN                  ! line  3   printed "F STUP"
        LV,$4,FADC                   ! line  4
        LC,$4,FALOC                  ! line  5
        BXCZ,KSUPP                   ! line  6
        B,FCKBT+.32                  ! line  7
FCKBT   V+,$3,FOVF                   ! line  8   printed "F CKBT"
        BB,FPTWD($3),FSVI            ! line  9
        V+I,$4,1.0                   ! line 10
        B,FCKBT                      ! line 11
FSVI    KVI,$0,0.0                   ! line 12   printed "F SVI"
        BXE,FSTN                     ! line 13
        L(BU),SIT($4)                ! line 14   printed "L(BU),SIT($4)"
        KF(BU,64),FWIT-20.($4)       ! line 15
        BZAE,FSVT                    ! line 16
        L(BU),0                      ! line 17
FSVT    ST(BU,64),1.0($2)            ! line 18   printed "F SVT"
FSTN    L(BU),1.0($1)                ! line 19 * printed "F STN"
        BRZ,FSTZ                     ! line 20
        BZB,9.24,FSBD                ! line 21
        KFI(BU,5),16,4               ! line 22
        BAE,FERRY                    ! line 23
        KFI(BU,9),64,4               ! line 24
        BAE,FERRY                    ! line 25
FINS    ST(BU),SIT($4)               ! line 26   printed "F INS"
FBTCK   V+I,$2,1.0                   ! line 27   printed "F BTCK"
        V+I,$1,1.0                   ! line 28
        CB+,$4,FCKBT                 ! line 29
        B,KSUPP                      ! line 30
FSTZ    TI,1,FWIT-20.($4),SIT($4)    ! line 31   printed "F STZ"
        B,FBTCK                      ! line 32
FSBD    KFI(BU,9),64,36              ! line 33   printed "F SBD"
        BZAE,FINS                    ! line 34
FERRY   LVI,$14,SFIXP                ! line 35   printed "F ERRY"
        B,FBIER                      ! line 36 *
FERRZ   BADZ,$.32                    ! line 37   printed "F ERRZ"
FERRX   LVI,$14,SFORBD               ! line 38   printed "F ERRX"
FBIER   SIC,SDISIC                   ! line 39   printed "F BIER"
        B,SDISP                      ! line 40   the SIC/branch pair, both on page
!                                    ! line 41   comment card, a lone "-"
FPTWD   DD(BU),0                     ! line 42   printed "F PTWD"
FBMSK   DD(BU),(16)BFFFFFF0000       ! line 43   SUBSTITUTE for "(16)DD(BU),BFFFFFF0000"
FALOC   VF,0.0                       ! line 44   printed "F ALOC"
FLZCN   VF,0.0                       ! line 45   printed "F LZCN"
FADC    VF,0.0                       ! line 46   printed "F ADC"
FOVF    VF,0.01                      ! line 47   printed "F OVF"
        CNOP                         ! line 48   emits NOTHING, counter aligned
FWIT    SIC,STIC                     ! line 49   printed "F WIT"
        BD,SIPT+20.                  ! line 50
        SIC,STIC                     ! line 51
        BD,SIFAE                     ! line 52
        SIC,STIC                     ! line 53
        BD,SIPT+22.                  ! line 54
        SIC,STIC                     ! line 55
        BD,SIPT+23.                  ! line 56   HALF word: counter leaves at 220650.00

